  <entry>
    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.16217v1</id>
    <title>WorldDraft: If Code Builds the World, Can Video Models Just Render It?</title>
    <updated>2026-11-12T03:09:18Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.16217v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.16217v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Multimodal coding agents decouple 4D world construction from visual generation, repurposing video models from world generators toward generative renderers. This division of labor raises a fundamental question: if code builds the world, can video models just render it? A reliable generative renderer hinges on two complementary criteria: (i) world preservation, retaining prescribed 4D kinematics and camera paths; and (ii) visual realization, persistently binding text-specified target attributes over time. To evaluate this capability, we introduce WorldDraft, a benchmark of $432$ strictly paired test cases across $48$ executable 4D world families spanning six dynamic challenge categories. Under a $3 \times 3$ factorial design, WorldDraft orthogonally crosses draft granularity (abstract proxy to previs) and appearance alignment (neutral to conflicting) under identical dynamics. Extensive evaluations across $12$ representative models reveal that: (I) world preservation and visual realization remain in stark operational tension; (II) richer draft scaffolding anchors structure but paradoxically impairs appearance fidelity; and (III) conflicting source cues trigger severe source leakage (up to $64\%$), exposing fragile cross-modal disentanglement. To mitigate these bottlenecks, we propose WorldDraft-Primer, a plug-and-play visual prompting strategy that consistently improves both objectives across frozen video renderers. Together, WorldDraft and WorldDraft-Primer lay a foundation for bridging programmatic 4D simulation with video generation, advancing physically grounded generative rendering.</summary>
    <category term="cs.CV" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
    <published>2026-11-12T03:09:18Z</published>
    <arxiv:comment>Project: https://haroldchen19.github.io/WorldDraft-site/</arxiv:comment>
    <arxiv:primary_category term="cs.CV"/>
    <author>
      <name>Zhiyu Hou</name>
